    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "A written companion to video footage of outcrop scale faults in sandstone (deformation bands) from Arches National Park is combined with graphics depicting their map relations, interaction features, localization, microstructure, and permeability to illustrate the details and complexities of these structures which are important for understanding fluid flow in sandstone reservoirs and for reconstructing tectonic history.",
